# Security and observability

- Reuse approved authorization SDKs/middleware/sidecars; do not hand-roll access checks.
- Fail closed when authorization or trusted tenant context is unavailable.
- Propagate trace and request context across async, messaging, and service calls.
- Use the established structured logger; redact credentials, policies, identities, tenant data,
  payloads, and high-cardinality values.
- Keep secrets in Secrets Manager and workload identity. Never place plaintext secrets in code,
  prompts, test fixtures, Terraform state inputs, Helm values, or CI variables committed to Git.
- Preserve bounded retries, timeouts, cancellation, health, and graceful shutdown behavior.
